Sval: background layers placed outside their box are not decoded

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2068103 (mozilla-central 60cea03fa4e1,
69926e5b012a, Firefox 161), unchanged. ESR 153 does not carry it.
Gecko decoded every background-image layer of a visible element, even a
no-repeat layer positioned wholly outside the element. A page that
stacks dozens of large frames and parks all but one far off the box
(rosebikes.com's scroll animation) filled the surface cache, which
evicted and re-decoded the frames while released surfaces queued up
behind a blocked main thread, until memory ran out and the system froze.
The first commit factors out the background position computation; the
second uses it to skip decoding a layer that cannot paint. The new pref
image.decode.defer_if_not_visible, true by default, gates it.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 161.

